redfin 1091: /dev/redwood-voice, the call's PCM for userland (coder V2, 2026-11-14). BBA study B1/C2 stage 2.
- kern.sweet_voice_proxy 2 (new value; 0 default and 1 unchanged, read at a call's start): the 1090 proxy call, but the
  downlink frames (0x2000) go to read() of /dev/redwood-voice instead of the speakers' call ring, and write() feeds the
  uplink (0x2001) instead of the mic ring. Call mode (3 x 10 ms playback periods) stays on as in mode 1.
- New bsd/dev/sweet_voicedev.c: 16-bit mono 10 ms frames at 8/16 kHz; read blocks <= 200 ms (EAGAIN), 0 bytes when no
  call / the call ends; write takes PCM, > 200 ms queued is dropped; one opener (EBUSY), uid/gid 501, 0660; nobody open
  = silence both ways, logged once per call. ioctls 'v' 1 GET_STATE, 2 SET_RATE (next call), 3 GET_TIME (sample +
  mach time of the latest downlink ack), 4 GET_COUNTERS. Fixed SPSC rings, no allocation or sleeping on the data thread.
- Node made at boot (sweet_ufs.c after sweet_audio_init); idle unless a mode-2 call runs.

